WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
Start with the part you can observe.

00:12.000 --> 00:24.000
Follow the relationship as it changes.

00:24.000 --> 00:36.000
A boundary layer is the near-surface region where viscosity affects velocity. Surface and pressure conditions influence its development.

00:36.000 --> 00:48.000
Velocity is near zero at the wall in the standard no-slip model and approaches the outer flow farther away.

00:48.000 --> 01:00.000
Flow-state sorting

01:00.000 --> 01:12.000
This simplified flow picture leaves out turbulence and test conditions. Real values need a stated method.

